      "month": "2026-06",
      "hasDiff": true,
      "ai": {
        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "CLI waiting-room promotes ASCII logo when model picker collapses",
        "summary": "FreebuffModelSelector now emits onExpandedChange to mirror its collapsed state to WaitingRoomScreen. The waiting-room screen uses this to promote the compact wordmark to the full ASCII logo when the picker is collapsed on mid-height terminals (>= 26 rows), filling otherwise dead space. Covers cli/src/components/freebuff-model-selector.tsx and cli/src/components/waiting-room-screen.tsx. useLayoutEffect ensures the parent's logo decision settles before paint, preventing layout flicker on mount and toggle.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-14T16:14:41.106Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When you open the CLI and the model picker is collapsed on a terminal at least 26 rows tall, the full ASCII logo now appears above the waiting room instead of the compact text logo. The picker reports its collapsed/expanded state to the screen, and useLayoutEffect ensures the logo decision settles before paint so there's no flicker on first load or when toggling. You'd just notice that the bigger logo shows up in the freed-up space when the model list is tucked away.",
